          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: Around 1 a.m., the witness observed orange-red lights taking different trajectories as they gained altitude and then faded away. The observation of several orange-red lights moving slowly for several minutes, towards the end of the weekend evening, clearly suggests Thai lanterns. Weather reports indicate a very light and unstable wind at that time. Therefore, the local wind is undetermined and subject to multiple variable influences. This wind pattern allows for nearly random movements of objects carried by the wind, according to temporary local breezes. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\": probable observation of Thai lanterns.",
